sources.notes:
Pages show LUX Center for the Arts offers gas reduction firing opportunities via membership, fellowship, and firing service. No wood, soda, salt, raku, or pit/barrel/saggar firings are mentioned. No dated workshops, classes, or crew calls for firings within the specified timeframe were found. The ceramic classes listed (wheel throwing, handbuilding, sculpture) do not explicitly state firing components in their course descriptions on the available pages.",
    "place_summary": "LUX Center for the Arts in Lincoln, Nebraska operates a gas reduction kiln (cone 10) available to studio members, fellows, and the public through a firing service. Outside potters can access this kiln via monthly studio membership ($120/month with gas reduction access), a work-exchange fellowship (currently waitlisted), or per-piece firing service.",
    "firing_evidence": [
      {
        "firing_type": "gas_reduction",
        "sentence": "Studio Members receive access to participate in community cone 10 gas reduction firings.",
        "quote": "Access to participate in community cone 10 gas reduction firings. Cone 10 clay can be purchased through the LUX, glazes are provided."
      }
    ]
